+## Ownership Boundary
+
+React owns only the stable Input/Button markup, Tend UI presentation and accessible names.
+
+`src/features/filters/filter-drawer.js` remains the sole owner of:
+
+- parsing and Russian currency formatting;
+- rounding by the `10,000` step;
+- clamping to `0..20,000,000`;
+- resolving crossed lower and upper boundaries;
+- active preset state;
+- track fill and range-thumb synchronization;
+- draft settings count;
+- Close, Reset and Apply side effects.
+
+The adapter has no `onChange`, `onClick`, filter state or direct product rerender.
+
+## Native Thumb Decision
+
+The two native `input[type="range"]` controls remain intentionally local.
+
+Tend UI contains `RangeInput`, but its local source contract describes two numeric input fields. It is not a dual-thumb slider and cannot replace the current drag interaction without removing behavior or adding a new local slider implementation.
+
+F-45 therefore treats the native thumbs as preserved product mechanics rather than unresolved legacy fields.
+
